cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GraphInstruct: A Progressive Benchmark for Diagnosing Capability Gaps in LLM Graph Generation"
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite the work below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "The GraphInstruct Authors"
abstract: >-
  GraphInstruct is a progressive-complexity benchmark for diagnosing where
  LLM graph-generation capability fails. It comprises 800 hand-authored
  instructions stratified into 6 complexity levels (L0-L5), 1,582
  algorithmically synthesized reference solutions, 4,163 distributional
  reference graphs, and 5 evaluation dimensions (D1 structural, D2 textual,
  D3 embedding, D4 instruction-match, D5 efficiency) using deterministic,
  LLM-as-judge-free metrics. A 12-LLM x 4-strategy capability survey
  (180,000 outputs) reveals where in the complexity spectrum each LLM
  breaks down, and complementary verification-guided generation methods
  (VGIG, CAAP) surpass the per-level prompt-engineering oracle by +0.035 to
  +0.050 on three target models.
license: MIT
license-url: "https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT"
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - graph generation
  - large language models
  - LLM evaluation
  - diagnostic benchmark
  - progressive complexity
  - structured generation
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-06"
